> carmu'u to one city from another?

It rotates, but I'm not sure of the connection between the rotation and=20
the translational movement of a tornado. carjevmu'u perhaps

  It seems that klama and muvdu
> involve a change in position as a change of location, rather than a
> change in position as a change of posture.

I'm not sure why this is necessarily so.  They refer to distinct origin=20
and destination places, and a route.  If all those can be specified=20
meaningfully, I'm not sure translational movement is required.

But then I'm not sure that there is no translation, anyway.  Turning=20
would be a translation in polar coordinates of the direction of facing.=20
  The object does not translate, but its facing does.


